# Added 2026-08-22, and this push is bought by a RULER rather than by any member's own number. On
# 2026-08-22 `gradeswap` scored 0.933 — a new best, one named swap off `sevenplane` (depth_regions_narrow
# out, grade_ladder in) chosen on ORDINAL CONCORDANCE and pre-registered on knee-7d1 before the number:
# above 0.932 confirms that ruler and licenses re-ranking every seat by it. It read 0.933. The other two
# rulers pointed elsewhere on the same swap — binary seat value priced it +0.0001 (a fifteenth of its own
# resolution, blind) and residual distance called grade_ladder the most redundant member of all 23 and
# predicted a LOSS.
#
# So the seats were re-ranked, and the scan is what makes this a push rather than a kernel edit: over all
# 67 same-split checkpoints, the FIVE HIGHEST ordinal members that are not already mounted are exactly
# these five, and the best MOUNTED unseated candidate (calibrated_targets, 0.776) beats the champion's
# weakest seat (lr4e-5_ws, 0.770) by only +0.006 — half the +0.011 gap that just bought a board tick.
# `small_accum` beats it by +0.014, larger than the gap that PASSED. The mounted pool's ordinal top is
# already seated; without this push the licensed move cannot be made at all.
#
# Read the seat numbers on these with the compression, not raw: `small_batch6` is +0.0005 offline against
# the shipped seven, which at knee-7d1's median +4.67 board points per holdout point is about +0.002 on
# the board. The morning's interpretation called 63 such candidates "exhausted" by comparing +0.0005
# straight against the +0.0015 BOARD threshold; gradeswap refutes that by instance (+0.0001 offline,
# +0.001 board) and both that document and the README are corrected. The pool is FLAT, not empty.
#
# THE CONSTANT ABOVE IS STALE, CORRECTED 2026-08-24, AND THE LINE IS LEFT STANDING SO THE CORRECTION HAS
# SOMETHING TO ATTACH TO. +4.67 was fitted over five or six pairs spanning 0.0043 offline — inside our own
# 0.0062 noise floor, so a slope through noise. The `weakseven` instrument (0.8562 offline, 0.908 board)
# placed a point outside that band and the refit read +2.14. So `small_batch6`'s +0.0005 prices at about
# +0.001 board, not the +0.002 written above, and EVERY offline delta converted anywhere in this file is
# worth 46% of what it was sold for. The RULE — never read an offline seat against a board threshold
# without the compression — stands unchanged; only the constant halved. Read it from `board_transfer`,
# never from prose, this comment included.
#
# AND THE CORRECTION ITSELF WAS WRONG, RE-CORRECTED HOURS LATER ON 2026-08-24, WHICH IS WHY THE LINE
# ABOVE ALSO STAYS. +2.14 was computed BY HAND from the prose ledger, because `comp/board.jsonl` — the
# file `board_transfer` actually reads — had gone unwritten since 2026-08-20 and was missing seven
# entries. One of its three anchors paired `gradeswap`'s offline 0.8694 with `finalfit`'s board 0.934:
# two different entries, and `finalfit` has no offline number at all, being six-sevenths `--fold -1`.
# Backfilled, the tool reads +1.92 over 15 entries and 90 pairs, and the inversion clause strengthened
# to 0 of 57 resolved pairs. The numeric move is small (2.14 → 1.92) and that is precisely why nothing
# caught it. Note also that the four best entries are one-sided and enter no pair, so +1.92 is fitted
# entirely at or below board 0.933 and is an EXTRAPOLATION where we now live at 0.937. The constant has
# been wrong twice and both times it was quoted from prose — including from this comment. Run
# `python -m kneemri.evaluation.board_transfer`; if it disagrees with any document, the document is stale.
# UNMOUNTED 2026-08-24 — vjepa_warm_s2026.pt, 0.8337, the most DISTANT member this project has produced.
# The line below stood since it was written, but the member was never actually in the live package, so
# the mismatch cost nothing and hid its own price. Packaging it for real today revealed the price:
# every kernel that loads the whole package then needs the VJEPA2 encoder mounted, and SIX do not
# declare it (efficient, loadcheck, solo, trained, trio, views, vote all flip to REFUSED in
# `mount_check`). Shipping this member was never a push, it was a push plus six kernel edits.
#
# Against that: it is 1.3 GB — fifteen ordinary members — and it does not seat. Today's displacement
# sweep (knee-98y2) ran nineteen candidates against the 8-member peak under exhaustive best-8 and this
# was one of them; the peak came back unchanged. It is also the FIRST of the three failures the roster
# itself records under knee-053z's distance-to-seat inference, quoted twenty lines below as the
# cautionary case `margin_seat` has to answer. Mounting the cautionary case was the inconsistency.
#
# Reversible, and the way back is written down: declare dimiturnt/vjepa2-hf/vjepa2-vitl on the six
# kernels above, then restore this line. Not done today because nothing measured wants the member.
# vjepa_warm_s2026.pt         # 0.8337 — the most DISTANT member this project has ever produced
# Added 2026-08-24, and it is the first member here whose encoder is not a 2D image trunk at all:
# V-JEPA2-large, a tubelet transformer that tokenises TWO slices per token, warm-started from our own
# 2D weights. Every other line in this file reads the volume one slice at a time and reconstructs depth
# afterwards; this one is handed the stack.
#
# Its solo number is the second-worst in the file and its seat value is +0.0002 — 0 of 1 clearing the
# +0.0015 BOARD_RESOLVABLE threshold, which by this roster's own rule means the offline ruler cannot
# tell it from the incumbent. That is the whole argument for mounting it, not against. Its
# nearest-neighbour correlation is 0.8210 against a seated band of 0.8801 to 0.9143, so it sits
# 0.06-0.09 further out than anything that has ever held a seat, and the quantity our holdout is known
# to misprice is exactly that distance (0.0059 offline became 0.014 on the board, 2.4x; knee-nas5,
# knee-avzz). `calib_span` at -0.0020 carried 0.929 and `through_dense` at -0.0020 is seated in the
# champion; this is the same shape with a larger step and a worse solo score.
#
# What it is NOT mounted on is its own arm's verdict. `vjepa_member` — the same trunk cold from natural
# video — read 0.8343 against a 0.845 bar and the mechanism is named: video pretraining teaches temporal
# object permanence and camera motion, and an MRI stack's third axis is anatomical depth with no motion
# at all. The warm start is the residue that null left standing, and its 0.8337 says the warm start did
# not rescue the solo score either. Neither number is a reason to expect a good MEAN from it.
#
# Mounting it required publishing the weights: `vjepa2l` carried no Kaggle mount until today, which is
# the half `knee-rpkw`'s recorded shippability clearance missed — it verified the kit carried the CODE
# and concluded the member could fire, while a kernel has no internet and reaches an encoder only
# through a mount, so `package_members.shippable` would have refused this line. Now
# `dimiturnt/vjepa2-hf/vjepa2-vitl`, the same private per-variant pattern as `dimiturnt/dinov3-hf`.
#
# NAMING IT IS GATED, and the gate is already running. `kneemri-augseat` tests whether the board pays
# for a member the offline ruler killed. At >= 0.940 that licenses mounting on distance against the
# ruler's verdict, and this is the strongest such candidate on the board by a wide margin. At <= 0.935
# the ruler was right and no kernel should name this. The line is added ahead of the answer only
# because mounting is reversible and a slot is not — the same reason every negative-delta member above
# was mounted before it was named.
margin_seat_s2026.pt        # 0.8525 — the first member measured into STRONG-AND-DISTANT, and the loss bought it
# Added 2026-08-24. `band_dense`'s recipe with the ranking loss replaced by an AUC-margin surrogate
# (`--auc-margin 1.0 --rank-weight 0.0`, single variable verified in the checkpoint's own config stamp).
# Solo 0.8525 against that control's 0.8578 is −0.0053, INSIDE the 0.0062 floor, so on quality this
# member is not distinguishable from the recipe it varies.
#
# It is mounted on the OTHER ruler, and unlike every negative-delta line above it clears the threshold
# rather than being excused from it. Greedy forward selection over 65 fold-0 records / 909 shared studies
# takes it SECOND of sixty-five — `small_batch6` 0.8598 → 0.8669, +0.0071 to the pair, the largest single
# addition in that curve. Priced against the resulting greedy-7 it is +0.0015 to add and +0.0013 to swap
# (displacing `crop80_span`). +0.0015 is exactly BOARD_RESOLVABLE; the tool's own line reads `0 of 3
# clear +0.0015`, so it sits ON the threshold, not past it. Against the historical distribution it is an
# order up: the best move across 59 candidates was +0.0004, and the mounted pool was written up as
# EXHAUSTED at +0.0002.
#
# WHY THIS LINE IS DIFFERENT FROM `vjepa_warm` ABOVE, which is the objection it has to answer. Both are
# mounted on distance. knee-053z has failed the distance-to-seat inference three times — `vjepa_warm`
# (most distant member we own, seat +0.0001), `gradeswap` (called most redundant, took a board tick), and
# `MemberCurve.diverse` (whose first five seats include `quarter_data` and `half_data`). The recorded
# reason is a confound, in the bead's own words: every distant member we own is distant partly by being
# bad. This one breaks it. Same trunk, same data, same recipe, same read — distance bought by the
# OBJECTIVE, at a solo cost inside the noise floor. Nearest-neighbour agreement 0.8628 against the greedy
# roster's own internal spread of 0.8717–0.8893, i.e. further from every seated member than any two of
# them are from each other, while `cnx_dense` (0.7686 nearest, 0.7927 solo) is what distant-and-weak looks
# like.
#
# The per-label profile is a redistribution, not a depression — MCL +0.0272*, Fracture +0.0250, Baker's
# +0.0163* against Lateral Meniscus −0.0546*, PF OA −0.0288*, Medial Meniscus −0.0277* — which is a
# DIFFERENT error structure rather than a worse one, and is the property a seat is actually bought with.
#
# Read the seat number with the compression and read the compression from the tool: `board_transfer` on
# 2026-08-24 says +1.92 board points per holdout point over 15 entries and 90 pairs, so +0.0013 prices at
# about +0.0025 board — and the tool also prints that +1.92 is fitted entirely at or below board 0.933
# while we now live at 0.937, so this is an extrapolation. Not claimed as an edge.
#
# Ledger row and full write-up: experiments/README.md, `margin_seat` — a losing solo that greedy picks
# SECOND of sixty-five. Mounting is reversible and a slot is not; naming it is a separate decision.
sided_pool_s2026.pt         # 0.8561 — seated in the greedy PEAK and never shippable until now
crop80_span_s2026.pt        # 0.8466 — the weakest member of that peak, seated on distance alone
# Added 2026-08-24, and the reason they are added is a SHIPPING HOLE rather than a new measurement.
# The 8-member greedy peak (0.8731, the best ensemble this project has measured) is
# small_batch6 + margin_seat + calib_span + through_dense + band_dense_long + sided_pool +
# aprior_dense + crop80_span. Five of those eight were in the live package; `margin_seat` was rostered
# but not yet pushed (knee-g6md), and these two had never been in the roster at all — `sided_pool`
# appears nowhere in this file before today and `crop80_span` only inside a comment on the line above,
# as the member `margin_seat` displaces. So our best measured ensemble has NEVER been submittable, and
# no board entry has ever contained it. That is the hole; the two lines close it.
#
# They are mounted on OPPOSITE rulers, which is what makes both worth the bytes. Measured over the peak
# eight, nearest-neighbour agreement runs 0.8628–0.8893. `sided_pool` reads solo 0.8561 — third best of
# the eight — at nearest 0.8879, which is the second CLOSEST seat in the set: it is there on quality,
# not on distance. `crop80_span` is the mirror image, solo 0.8466 (the WEAKEST of the eight) at nearest
# 0.8717, the second most distant seat after `margin_seat`'s 0.8628: it is there on distance alone, and
# the greedy took it over members half a point better on quality.
#
# NOT claimed: that either improves a board entry. The peak is a holdout reading, `board_transfer`'s
# +1.92 points-per-holdout-point is fitted at or below 0.933 while we sit at 0.937, and the whole
# ninth-seat sweep (knee-98y2, 33 candidates) says this set resists addition and single-swap. What is
# claimed is narrower and sufficient: an ensemble we can measure but cannot upload is an ensemble we
# cannot test, and mounting is reversible where a slot is not.
final_ws_e12.pt             # THE DARK MEMBER — no offline score exists or can exist
# Added 2026-08-23. band_dense's flags copied verbatim plus --fold -1 and --ema, so it trains on 4,406
# studies rather than 3,497. It has SEEN every holdout study: it can never be seat-scored, curve-scored
# or distance-scored, and it must never enter a pool that reports an offline mean. knee-7d1's 4.67x
# board-per-holdout compression does not apply to it either — that converts an HONEST offline delta, and
# this member has none. It ships blind against the pinned 0.933 in `kneemri-finalfit` or not at all.
calib_span_ff.pt            # DARK. calib_span_s2026's flags plus --fold -1 --ema
grade_ladder_ff.pt          # DARK. grade_ladder_s2026's flags plus --fold -1 --ema
through_dense_ff.pt         # DARK. through_dense_s2026's flags plus --fold -1 --ema
lr4e-5_ws_ff.pt             # DARK. lr4e-5_ws_s2026's flags plus --fold -1 --ema
base_dense_ff.pt            # DARK. base_dense_s2026's flags plus --fold -1 --ema (variant base, batch 6)
# Added 2026-08-24, from final_fit_six.sh members 1-5. Every caveat on final_ws_e12 above applies to all
# five WITHOUT EXCEPTION: they have seen every holdout study, no offline score exists or can exist for
# them, they must never enter a pool that reports an offline mean, and no board-per-holdout compression
# converts anything about them because they have no honest offline delta to convert.
#
# The sixth member of that arm, band_dense_long_ff, DOES NOT EXIST and is not expected to. The chain was
# stopped before it (logs/YIELD_CARD, 2026-08-24 06:19Z) because final_fit_six.sh's own header gates the
# whole arm on kneemri-finalfit reading 0.936 and it read 0.934. Its seat is filled by the fold-0
# band_dense_long_s2026, which is what makes `kneemri-allfit` a six-of-seven swap rather than a clean
# sweep — stated here because an entry whose composition looks like an oversight will be read as one.
#
# Added 2026-08-24 23:06Z, ahead of the run finishing, so the reset window is fire-only.
small_batch6_ff.pt          # DARK. small_batch6_s2026's flags plus --fold -1 --ema. The SEVENTH dark
# member and the first one that has ever existed; count-of-dark-members was held at six by every board
# entry since finalfit because six was all there were. Every caveat above applies without exception: it
# has seen every holdout study, no offline score exists or can exist for it, and it must never enter a
# pool that reports an offline mean. Its fold-0 twin small_batch6_s2026 is greedy seat 1 of 67 (0.8598)
# and held the swapped seat in lastseat at 0.937, so this member's behaviour is a measured control.
